 "notes": "Four OCR'd plates: 1 geologic map, 2 cross sections A-A' to E-E', 3 tectonic map, 4 metamorphic isograds. Units listed in the explanation with no stratigraphic order implied and no descriptions or ages; grouped as Non-migmatitic belt and Walhalla Nappe. Plate 2 names mfq 'Micaceous and amphibole gneiss', Plate 1 'Micaceous feldspathic quartzite' (both kept). Sections read from page images: end labels, elevation units and a few unit labels; the drawn contacts, reverse faults and folds were not digitized (section lengths and distance scale not printed beyond the bar scale). Plate 3 fold axes and Plate 4 kyanite and hornblende isograds are drawn but carry no values beyond names. No drill holes or references. SUBSURFACE: section contacts and reverse faults drawn but not digitized.",
